# Synergien first-class (never orphan)

Live product has **two** equal Pages surfaces:

- Builder: https://lzra2000.github.io/aldi-buildschmiede/
- Synergien: https://lzra2000.github.io/aldi-buildschmiede/synergien.html

Any website / visual / chrome / tokens / a11y / nav / assemble / site-docs ship must treat Synergien as **first-class with the builder**. Do not ship Builder-only chrome and leave Synergien behind.

## When you touch Builder chrome — also Synergien

If you change any of:

- shared CSS tokens / colors / typography / spacing
- header, brand, nav, footer, a11y landmarks
- site-wide visual language (panels, borders, original chrome)
- assemble behavior that affects shipped HTML

…then you **must** also:

1. Update `src/synergien-source.html` in the same ship (mirror tokens/nav/chrome as needed; Synergien may keep school-only hues).
2. Keep **bidirectional nav**: Builder ↔ Synergien links stay present and correct (`index.html` ↔ `synergien.html`).
3. Run `python3 pipeline/assemble.py` — it **always** writes both `index.html` **and** `synergien.html`.
4. Commit **both** rebuilt artifacts when they change.

Agents inventing original chrome (see `website-assets.mdc`) apply that freedom to **both** pages — not Builder alone.

## Lanes

| Surface | Source | Built artifact |
|---|---|---|
| Builder | `src/builder-head.html`, `builder-body.html`, `builder-app.js` | `index.html` |
| Synergien | `src/synergien-source.html` | `synergien.html` |

`pipeline/assemble.py` copies/emits Synergien every run; missing `src/synergien-source.html` is a hard fail. Never hand-edit root `synergien.html` in parallel with source edits.

## Never

- Ship token/chrome/nav/a11y changes only in Builder sources
- Drop or orphan Synergien from nav, README live links, or assemble
- Assume Pages updates from a local assemble without commit+push of **both** HTML ships
